    "q-164375": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164375",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the hyperboloid of two sheets $-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=-1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperboloid. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{0}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{z}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a hyperbola in $xz$-plane.",
